  "title": "90: Al-Balad البلد",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nلَاۤ اُقْسِمُ بِهٰذَا الْبَلَدِۙ‏(1)\nLAA UQSEMO BE-HAAZAL BALADE.\nNay! Swear I by this City (Mecca)!\nوَاَنْتَ حِلٌّ ۢ بِهٰذَا الْبَلَدِۙ‏(2)\nWA ANTA HILLUM BE-HAAZAL BALADE.\nWhile thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) hath been settler in this City!\nوَوَالِدٍ وَّمَا وَلَدَ ۙ‏(3)\nWA WAALEDINW WA MAA WALADA.\nAnd the Begetter (Adam) and whom he begat (mankind)\nلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ فِىْ كَبَدٍؕ‏(4)\nLAQAD KHALAQNAL INSAANA FEE KABAD.\nIndeed We have created man (to dwell) amidst hardship\nاَيَحْسَبُ اَنْ لَّنْ يَّقْدِرَ عَلَيْهِ اَحَدٌ ۘ‏(5)\nA-YAHSABO AL LAN-Y YAQDERA A’LAYHE AHAD.\nWhat! Thinketh he that over him none, ever hath (any) power?\nيَقُوْلُ اَهْلَكْتُ مَالًا لُّبَدًا ؕ‏(6)\nYAQOOLO AHLAKTO MAALAL LOBADAA.\nSaith he: ‘‘I have wasted, wealth enormous!\nاَيَحْسَبُ اَنْ لَّمْ يَرَهٗۤ اَحَدٌ ؕ‏(7)\nA-YAHSABO AL LAM YARAHU AHAD.\nWhat! Thinketh he that no one seeth him?\nاَلَمْ نَجْعَلْ لَّهٗ عَيْنَيْنِۙ‏(8)\nALAM NAJ-A’L LAHU A’YNAYNE.\nWhat! Made We not for him, (his) two eyes?\nوَلِسَانًا وَّشَفَتَيْنِۙ‏(9)\nWA LESAANANW WA SHAFATAYNE.\nAnd a tongue and two lips\nوَهَدَيْنٰهُ النَّجْدَيْنِۚ‏(10)\nWA HADAYNAAHUN NAJDAYN.\nAnd we showed him the two high-ways (of good and evil)\nفَلَا اقْتَحَمَ الْعَقَبَةَۖ‏(11)\nFALAQ TAHAMAL A’QABAH.\nBut he strove not unto (crossing over) the Ascent steep\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا الْعَقَبَةُ ؕ‏(12)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAL A’QABAH.\nWhat would make thee know what is the Ascent steep?\nفَكُّ رَقَبَةٍ ۙ‏(13)\nFAKKO RAQABATIN.\n(It is) the freeing a slave or a captive\nاَوْ اِطْعٰمٌ فِىْ يَوْمٍ ذِىْ مَسْغَبَةٍ ۙ‏(14)\nAW IT-A’AMUN FEE YAWMIN ZEE MASGHABATIN-Y.\nOr feeding in the day of hunger\nيَّتِيْمًا ذَا مَقْرَبَةٍ ۙ‏(15)\nYATEEMAN ZAA MAQRABATIN.\nTo an Orphan, being near of kin\nاَوْ مِسْكِيْنًا ذَا مَتْرَبَةٍ ؕ‏(16)\nAW MISKEENAN ZAA MATRABAH.\nOr to the poor one lying in the dust\nثُمَّ كَانَ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَتَوَاصَوْا بِالصَّبْرِ وَتَوَاصَوْا بِالْمَرْحَمَةِ ؕ‏(17)\nSUMMA KAANA MENAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA TAWAASAW BIS-SABRE WA TAWAASAW BIL MARHAMAH.\nBesides this, to be of those who believe, and enjoin steadfastness on each other, and enjoin mercy on each other\nاُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْمَيْمَنَةِ ؕ‏(18)\nOOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUL MAYMANAH.\nThese are the people of the Right Hand\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا هُمْ اَصْحٰبُ الْمَشْئَمَةِ ؕ‏(19)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-AAYAATENA HUM ASHAABUL MASH-AMAH.\nAnd those who disbelieve in Our signs, they are the people of the Left Hand\nعَلَيْهِمْ نَارٌ مُّؤْصَدَةٌ‏(20)\nA’LAYHIM NAARUM MOOSADAH.\nOn them shall be the fire closed over",
  "merits": "Surah al-Balad (The City)\nThis Surah has 20 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that whoever recites this Surah will be safe from the Wrath of Allah (s.w.t.) on the Day of Reckoning. Those who recite this Surah in their obligatory prayers, will be counted among the pious and will given a highly status in the company of the Prophets and martyrs.\nWriting this Surah as a talisman and tying it around the neck of a child keeps him safe from illness. Water on which this Surah has been dissolved, if put in the nostrils, acts as a cure for nose ailments."
